Raspberry Pi OS Installation Guide

This guide outlines the steps to install Raspberry Pi OS on a Raspberry Pi 4 for headless (remote) access via SSH.
Prerequisites

    Raspberry Pi 4

    MicroSD card (8GB minimum, 16GB+ recommended)

    Computer with SD card reader

    Network connection for initial setup

Installation Steps
1. Prepare Installation Medium

    Install Raspberry Pi Imager

        Download from raspberrypi.com/software

        Available for Windows, macOS, and Linux

    Insert SD Card

        Insert the microSD card into your computer's card reader

2. Configure and Write OS Image

    Launch Raspberry Pi Imager

    Select Device: Choose "Raspberry Pi 4"

    Choose OS: Select "Raspberry Pi OS (other)" → "Raspberry Pi OS Lite" (or your preferred variant)

    Select Storage: Choose your inserted SD card

    Configure Settings (Click gear icon or Ctrl+Shift+X):

        Enable SSH: Set password authentication

        Configure Wi-Fi (optional for wireless setup):

            Enter SSID and password

            Select your country

        Set username and password

        Configure locale settings if needed

    Write Image: Click "WRITE" and confirm to begin writing

3. Boot Raspberry Pi

    Eject SD card safely from your computer

    Insert SD card into Raspberry Pi 4

    Connect power to boot the Raspberry Pi

    Wait 1-2 minutes for initial boot process to complete

4. Remote Access

    SSH Access: Connect using your computer's terminal:
    bash

ssh username@raspberrypi.local

or use the IP address if known:
bash

ssh username@[IP_ADDRESS]
